class.description:
[CgameBVH] builds a binned surface-area-heuristic bounding volume hierarchy over a triangle soup and answers closest-hit and any-hit ray queries using the Moller-Trumbore ray/triangle test. It is the acceleration structure used by [CgamePathTracer], and is also usable on its own for line-of-sight checks and picking against baked geometry.
Queries do not modify the hierarchy and are safe to call from several threads at once, as long as no thread calls [method build] or [method clear] at the same time.
[codeblock]
var tris := PackedVector3Array([
    Vector3(-10, 0, -10), Vector3(-10, 0, 10), Vector3(10, 0, 10),
])
var bvh := CgameBVH.new()
bvh.build(tris)
var hit := bvh.intersect(Vector3(0, 5, 0), Vector3.DOWN)
if hit["hit"]:
    print("Hit triangle ", hit["tri"], " at distance ", hit["t"])
[/codeblock]
